# Project Engineering Standards

- Inspect the repository structure before implementing changes.
- Read package.json and tsconfig.json when available.
- Follow existing architecture and naming conventions.
- Prefer simple, maintainable solutions.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies and abstractions.
- Keep changes scoped to the requested task.
- Use strict TypeScript when applicable.
- Validate untrusted inputs at system boundaries.
- Never expose credentials or secrets.
- Add tests for meaningful behavior changes.
- Run available lint, typecheck and test commands.
- Never claim tests passed unless executed.
- Do not execute destructive commands without approval.
- Summarize modified files and validation results.
